{
	title: 'Cache-preserving named prompt sections',
	spec: 'Implement tasks/q5g/sections.md: named matching-colon sections in SYSTEM.md, whole or diff updates in hal-notes, cache-preserving fork and lifecycle behavior, local instructions through $agents, explicit template errors and advisory imitation warnings. This supersedes the deferred/updatable proposals. Preserve the hookable assembly contract from task ar.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Build <updatable> inside systemPrompt.assemble(input, sources, problems), the single hookable function that builds the prompt (09-mob, task ar): prompt-trail.ts diffs the unhooked original (plugins.state.patches) against systemPrompt.inspect().text, and prompt-files.ts watches the assemble hooks. If assemble is renamed or split, keep a hookable equivalent and update both files.',
		'Prompt-template parses nested matching-colon fences and records section spans through the same hookable systemPrompt.assemble snapshot; systemPrompt.agents owns the existing nearest-Git-root discovery and AGENTS.md-first/CLAUDE.md-fallback policy (the fallback is Hal-specific, not an AGENTS standard). Local skills and files expand literally inside $agents. prompt-cache stores frozen text, latest source rendering, and update cutoff in live-file-backed prompt.ason; a per-family last-request file evaluates one-hour inactivity only at requests. Forks inherit cacheId separately from actual auth/session identity. Updates are durable independently editable notices; comparing source state prevents deleted/edited notes from being silently repaired. Clear/compact and expiry omit superseded updates from provider input. Malformed templates keep the last valid prompt and standing complete errors; without one the raw template is recovery input. External tag imitation emits an advisory warning before output capping without changing the result.',
		'One-off measured repeated update cost: 20 single-line edits in 1,000-line/10,000-line sections took 264/576 ms total; 100 unchanged prepares took 174/1,027 ms. Last update notices stayed 109/110 bytes; persistent cache was 48,178/354,179 bytes (initial and latest rendering, not cumulative snapshots). Cache handles close with sessions, and no cache-expiry polling loop runs.',
		'Rebase keeps historical provider instructions solely in frozen system/history. Setting surgery captures a current rendered source baseline only to detect later genuine edits, never to restore instructions. After any rebase, genuine changes in diff sections also include the authoritative full replacement because edited/removed historical notes can make the old-side diff inapplicable; no update is emitted solely to repair a rebase. A full prompt rebuild clears this reconciliation state. Family inactivity persists an epoch, so every member rebuilds on its next request. Superseded section updates are omitted after replay/rebase projection, preserving numbered rebase targets. Standing template faults are broadcast only when changed. Regression tests cover all these invariants.',
		'Focused integration tests and typecheck/lint pass. Full-suite attempts retain complete output with nonzero status; unrelated dated legacy guards, module-size limits, request compression fixtures and browser/socket failures remain. e2e fixture framing now follows independently delivered hal-note context; its fake HTTP endpoint still rejects compressed provider bodies from the existing transport.',
		'Final scoped integration verification: 136 tests across 20 files pass, including cache expiry/rebase/source-baseline regressions, provider routing, pruning, settings recovery, both rebase clients and spawn-budget ownership; TypeScript, owned lint and diff whitespace checks pass. The full suite is not green; full outputs are retained and unrelated failures remain outside these tasks.',
		'User correction: tag-imitation warnings belong to the model, not the user. Preserve durable notice delivery through history.messages and unchanged tool output, but never broadcast a terminal/web warning banner. Regression verifies provider input contains the warning and client warning events do not.'
